---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '@/consts';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The terms governing your use of DevToolSDK: what you may do with our content, what our guides are and are not, and the limits of our liability."
  path="/terms"
  lead="Short, readable, and written to be understood rather than to be impossible to argue with."
>
  <h2 id="acceptance">1. Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    By using {SITE.name} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not
    use the site. These terms are governed by the laws of {LEGAL.jurisdiction}.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-this-is">2. What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} publishes educational guides about software tools, written and verified as
    described in our <a href="/about#how-we-write">editorial process</a>. Our guides are
    documentation and opinion, not professional advice.
  </p>
  <p>
    Specifically, nothing on this site constitutes legal, financial, security or procurement
    advice. A guide reflects the tool version stated at the top of the chapter, on the platforms
    we tested, which may differ from your environment in ways that change the outcome. Commands
    that modify systems, delete data or incur cloud costs are your responsibility to understand
    before you run them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accuracy">3. Accuracy and currency</h2>
  <p>
    Software changes, and command line flags change with it. We revisit guides when a release
    invalidates a chapter and mark them with an updated date, but we cannot guarantee that every
    command on every page works with the version you have installed. Always check the official
    documentation for the version you are running.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you find an error, <a href="/contact">tell us</a> — corrections get priority over
    everything else in our queue.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-use">4. Your use of our content</h2>
  <p>You may:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Read, print and share our articles for personal or internal business use</li>
    <li>Quote brief excerpts with clear attribution and a link to the original page</li>
    <li>Link to any page on this site, from anywhere, without asking</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You may not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Republish articles in whole or in substantial part without written permission</li>
    <li>Present our content as your own, or strip attribution from it</li>
    <li>Scrape the site at a volume that degrades it for other readers</li>
    <li>Use our content to train a model that reproduces it, without permission</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    All editorial content is © {LEGAL.entityName}. The source code of this website is available
    under the MIT license. Trademarks and product names belong to their respective owners, and
    their use here is nominative — it does not imply any affiliation or endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="submissions">5. What you send us</h2>
  <p>
    If you send us a comparison suggestion, a correction or any other feedback, you grant us a
    non-exclusive right to act on it, including publishing a correction that references it. We
    will not publish your name or contact details without asking you first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party">6. Third-party links and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to third-party websites and displays advertising served by Google. We do not
    control either, and we are not responsible for their content, their products or their privacy
    practices. A link is not an endorsement, and an advertisement is definitively not one — see
    our <a href="/disclosure">advertising and affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">7. Availability</h2>
  <p>
    We make no guarantee that the site will be available, uninterrupted or error-free. We may
    change, suspend or discontinue any part of it at any time without notice.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site and its content are provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, express or
    implied. To the fullest extent permitted by law, {LEGAL.entityName} is not liable for any
    indirect, incidental, consequential or punitive damages arising from your use of the site or
    from decisions made in reliance on its content.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law, including
    liability for fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy">9. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Your use of the site is also governed by our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, which
    explains what we collect and how advertising cookies work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">10. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The effective date at the top of this page always reflects the
    current version. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.<br />
    {LEGAL.entityName} — {LEGAL.location}.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
